# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      auth: false
      description: `Every public holiday in Japan since 1955, from Business Box (marubox.jp): English and Japanese names and the kind of holiday (national, substitute, citizens or special), edited from the Cabinet Office's official list. Static JSON files, no key, no sign-up, served with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *. Credit is required: "Source: Cabinet Office, Government of Japan. Edited by Business Box (marubox.jp)"; cache the files rather than fetching on every request.

Sources: the documentation page https://marubox.jp/holidays/, with both JSON files probed live on 2026-10-23 (all years, 2026, 1955, and 2030). On that date the data ran from 1955 to 2027 (1,067 holidays) and was last updated 2026-09-29.

Not modelled: the CSV (jp.csv) and iCalendar (jp.ics, jp-ja.ics) forms of the same data. A year outside the data (e.g. 2030) does not 404: the site answers HTTP 200 with an HTML page, so only years present in the data are valid.`
      servers: [
        {
          url: "https://marubox.jp/holidays"
        }
      ]
      summary: "Every public holiday in Japan since 1955, from Business Box (marubox.jp): English and Japanese names and the kind of holiday (national, substitute, citizens or special), edited from the Cabinet Office's official list."
      title: "Japanese Public Holidays"
      version: "1.0.0"
      website: "https://marubox.jp/holidays/"
    }
  }
}

